Author: Paulo Gomes <paulo@entire.io>
Date:   Thu Oct 15 15:34:55 2026 +0100

    pkg/policy: Storer-parameterized policy API

    gittuf's policy engine is parameterized by gitstore.Storer, but
    experimental/gittuf.Repository, the only way to reach it, is bound to an
    on-disk Git repository. Expose authoring, verification, and inspection
    over any Storer so external modules can drive gittuf trust over their
    own storage.

    Bootstrap authors a root and a top-level targets rule file, stages, and
    applies. Author writes the same metadata as a tree and stops there, so a
    caller doing its own commit, reference, and RSL handling can choose the
    commit's parent. VerifyRef, VerifyRefFromEntry, InspectRoot, and
    VerifyTransition cover the read side.

    InspectRoot takes WithEntry to bind the read to one RSL policy entry,
    and WithInitialRootKeys to anchor the first root rather than trust it on
    sight.

    Bootstrap needs exclusive write access to the policy and RSL references.
    It rolls back conditionally, reverting only the tips it recorded, and it
    reads those tips back because the engine does not report what it wrote.

    Keys cross the API as crypto.Signer and crypto.PublicKey, so no exported
    field names a gittuf internal type.

    internal/policy gains State.WriteTree, extracted from State.Commit.
